Feature: a role's answer reaches the pane that role is actually running in

  # BL-846 (defect, slice of BL-772). Answer delivery resolves role R's live
  # pane from the roles.tsv `session` column (swarmforge-QA for QA). Under
  # mono-router only the resident pane (swarmforge-coder) and the coordinator
  # pane exist, so for every rotating role the live-pane leg can never deliver
  # — even when that role IS the resident currently running in the resident
  # pane. Delivery always falls through to the queued-note leg, which a role
  # holding in-process work is forbidden to read ("Do NOT run
  # ready_for_next.sh again until you finish it"). The fix is resolution only:
  # consult the durable resident-identity marker that rotation already writes,
  # and resolve the resident pane for the role it names.
  #
  # PARKED AS .feature.draft per BL-233: this slice is not built, so a live
  # *.feature here would have no step handlers and would hard-fail the
  # acceptance runner for every other ticket. The coder renames this to
  # .feature and lands its step handlers in the same parcel.

  Background:
    Given a mono-router swarm whose only live panes are the resident pane and the coordinator pane
    And the roster names a distinct session for every pipeline role

  # BL-846 role-pane-resolution-follows-recorded-identity-01
  Scenario Outline: the live pane resolved for a role follows the recorded resident identity
    Given the resident identity marker is <marker>
    When delivery resolves the live pane for role "<requested role>"
    Then it resolves <resolution>

    Examples:
      | marker  | requested role | resolution                    |
      | "QA"    | QA             | the resident pane             |
      | "QA"    | cleaner        | cleaner's own session pane    |
      | "QA"    | coordinator    | coordinator's own session pane|
      | "coder" | coder          | the resident pane             |
      | "coder" | QA             | QA's own session pane         |
      | missing | QA             | QA's own session pane         |
      | blank   | QA             | QA's own session pane         |

  # BL-846 answer-interrupts-a-blocked-resident-02
  Scenario: an answer reaches a resident role that is blocked holding in-process work
    Given the resident identity marker is "QA"
    And QA has a clarifying question pending
    And QA holds in-process work
    When the human answers that question
    Then the answer is delivered into the resident pane as an interrupting nudge
    And no answer note is queued into QA's inbox
    And QA's pending question marker is cleared

  # BL-846 dormant-role-answer-still-queues-03
  Scenario: an answer for a role the resident is not running as still queues as a note
    Given the resident identity marker is "coder"
    And QA has a clarifying question pending
    When the human answers that question
    Then the answer is queued as a note into QA's inbox
    And QA's pending question marker is cleared
